Changelog: 30-10-2026 16:11:24

Release 2.0.0.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:53:19

Breaking. A game's Steam shortcut starts the app's play mode (owner, 30-10-2026: "Hold View + Menu, everywhere"):
Vita3K-Manager.exe --play -r <title ID>, which starts Vita3K in its folder and ends with it, so its Steam number and
artwork names change. A shortcut made before, which starts Vita3K.exe itself, is still the game's: it shows (Update
Steam), and Y Update Steam writes it again (shortcuts.outdated()).

Changelog: 30-10-2026 14:53:19

Added. Hold View and Menu together for two seconds to quit a game (core's play mode): Vita3K closes as its window
would, from Steam's library, X Play or without Steam, where Steam's Exit game was the only way out (it still works).
The line at the bottom says so when a game starts ("In the game, hold View and Menu together to quit."), and Your
games' information and the wiki chapter.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Breaking. The Open Steam row at the top of Your games is gone (owner, 30-10-2026): Steam's library opens from the
portal, RT Steam.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 13:35:58

Added. On a device without Steam (not installed, or never started), X Play starts the game in Vita3K itself, full
screen, with the command its Steam shortcut has (shortcuts.command(), core's platform.start_program() outside the
app's bundle; owner, 30-10-2026: a fallback, as a game cannot be played without Steam otherwise). Without Vita3K
installed it says to install it first. With Steam installed X plays through Steam as before.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 12:54:34

Fixed. Steam started by the app signs in (core, owner, 30-10-2026): X Play and the restart after Steam's shortcuts
changed started steam.exe by the lower-case name in Steam's registry key, and a Steam started so never signed in, its
login window off the screen; it is started by its name as on the disk now, outside the app's bundle. The information
popup's text box is as high as its text, up to 0.7 of the window: a text with "[PS Vita] <title>" in it was measured as
HTML and kept four lines high.

Changelog: 30-10-2026 01:30:27

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 23:14:12

Fixed. Update Steam starts Steam again signed in (core's with_steam_closed(): a plain steam.exe on Windows; owner,
29-10-2026): the steam.exe -silent it started never signed in, so a game's Play and Open Steam did nothing until
Steam was started by hand. The status line says Steam was started again, signed in.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:56:04

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 21:44:22

Added. X Play on a game of Your games that is in Steam starts it through Steam (steam://rungameid, Steam started
first when it does not run; owner, 29-10-2026: a game started from the manager); a game not in Steam yet says how it
gets there. Open Steam, a row at the top of Your games, opens Steam's library in Big Picture (A Open Steam). Every
browser of the app opens again in the folder last taken or picked a file in (core's browse.remembered), while it is
there.

Fixed. The Log pane's newest lines were a label that grew past the pane and was cut off at the top (owner,
29-10-2026): they are a view of their own now, its newest line in view, which a finger scrolls; a tap on it shows the
whole log as A does.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 20:26:55

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 29-10-2026 19:58:49

Added. The BC250 suite's Vita3K Manager on the portable window (owner, 29-10-2026: the gaming category, after
shadPS4 Manager), laid out as RPCS3 Manager: four cards, Vita3K, Your games, Settings and Log, the actions with a
controller button in the row at the bottom. A Install downloads Vita3K build 4186 for Windows, the build the BC250
suite's app pins (vita3k-4186-f0273e4c-windows-x86_64.7z from Vita3K/Vita3K-builds, 25 MB), checks it against the
pinned SHA-256 and unpacks it with Windows' own tar (a .7z, as RPCS3 Manager's) into
%LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-vita3k\emulator\ with Vita3K's portable folder portable\ beside
it, where Vita3K keeps its config.yml, its log and the PS Vita's storage, fs\ (build 4186's own rule: a portable folder
beside the program, else %APPDATA%\Vita3K\Vita3K); X Remove Vita3K, with a second press, deletes only its program; Y
Update when another build is there. The Vita3K pane says when Microsoft's Visual C++ runtime is missing (Vita3K.exe
imports vcruntime140, vcruntime140_1, msvcp140 and msvcp140_atomic_wait), which parts of the PS Vita's firmware are
installed, and when a newer Vita3K build is out (asked of GitHub when the window opens, the BC250 app's notice; the
build is never installed). LB Firmware: the app's folder browser in Downloads showing the .PUP files; A on one gives it
to Vita3K (--firmware), which installs it without a window, and the pane names the parts it wrote. RB Install a game:
the browser showing the .vpk, .zip and .pkg files. A on a .vpk or .zip, or X on a dumped game's own folder, gives it to
Vita3K, which installs it and then opens its window to start the game; the app closes Vita3K as soon as that window
shows (owner, 29-10-2026). A on a .pkg opens a page for its license key (the zRIF, X Paste), then Vita3K installs it
without a window (--pkg, --zrif); the key is in no log line. What came into Vita3K's storage (a game, an update, extra
content) is named on the status line. When the app installs Vita3K, opens and gives Vita3K a job, it sets three lines
of config.yml: games full screen, Vita3K's welcome window and its own update check off. Your games: the games
installed in Vita3K (ux0\app), read as the BC250 app reads them; played from Steam, never from the app (owner,
29-10-2026), as Vita3K.exe -r <ID>: Vita3K's own frontend boots the game full screen (owner, 29-10-2026: the BC250
app's SDL frontend opens a 960 x 544 window that never goes full screen on Windows); A Steam mark and Y Update Steam
put them in Steam as "[PS Vita] <title>" (Vita3K and its firmware installed first), with the game's own pictures and a
cover from SteamGridDB with the suite's key (RB Steam artwork). Settings in four tabs (Picture, Speed, Sound, System:
16 of config.yml's settings, which the BC250 app leaves to Vita3K's own window), never written while Vita3K runs. Log:
Vita3K's folder and the app's log, read in the app. Not carried over from the BC250 window: Play on the desktop and
Vita3K's own settings window.
